INT. OFFICE BREAK ROOM - MORNING

Fluorescent hum. A vending machine stuffed with a single bag of pretzels. A laminated sign: "WE ARE A FAMILY."

BRENDA SZABO (50s, lanyard, cardigan) stands at the coffee maker, stirring a cup that is already stirred. QUENTIN FAIRLEIGH (30s, ironed shirt) stares at his phone. RAVINDRA SHETTY (40s, headset, one earbud in) pours water on a dying plant. TESS OKAFOR-LUND (20s, intern, binder) hugs the wall.

Nobody talks. The coffee maker gurgles.

QUENTIN
Anyone get the memo?

BRENDA
Which one?

QUENTIN
The one about the other memo.

RAVINDRA
(not looking up)
I thought it was cancelled.

TESS
There's a memo?

Brenda and Quentin exchange a look. Then they study the pretzels.

The door opens. ARCHIBALD STONE (50s, tailored suit, a smile like a hospital bed) steps in. Everyone stiffens.

ARCHIBALD
Good morning, family.

ALL
(mumbled)
Morning.

Archibald crosses to the vending machine. Puts in a coin. The pretzels fall. He opens the bag.

ARCHIBALD
Tess, I hear you've been rearranging the supply closet.

TESS
I was told to--

ARCHIBALD
It's lovely. Truly. We should have a meeting about it.

Brenda drops her spoon. It clatters. Quentin sets his phone face down. Ravindra waters the plant again. It drowns.
